%% Solid = transition exists in the repo, cited. Red dashed class = a state whose
%% only exit is a human or a 180-day purge, i.e. no automatic exit.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> pending: createBatch inserts batch_items status pending<br/>batch.ts:127 · schema.ts:466

    pending --> queued: markQueued, guarded from pending|failed<br/>sets queued_at · batch.ts:267
    failed --> queued: retry action or DLQ replay<br/>batch/[id]/+page.server.ts:291 · admin/dead-letters:103

    queued --> extracting: markExtracting, guarded from queued|extracting<br/>batch.ts:306<br/>IDEMPOTENCY the guarded UPDATE is the only lock,<br/>pg-boss singletonKey = itemId queue.ts:66
    extracting --> done: markDone writes extracted_data<br/>extraction-worker.ts:413 · batch.ts:314
    extracting --> failed: markFailed with errorClass<br/>extraction-worker.ts:138 · batch.ts:328

    queued --> failed: stall reaper, queued_at older than<br/>EXTRACTION_STALL_TIMEOUT_MS 900000 ms<br/>batch.ts:283 · env.ts:23
    extracting --> failed: same reaper, IN_FLIGHT covers both<br/>batch.ts:62,294

    done --> confirmed: markConfirmed, only from done<br/>batch.ts:336, called after the invoice insert commits<br/>batch/[id]/+page.server.ts:305
    pending --> discarded: markDiscarded batch.ts:342
    queued --> discarded: markDiscarded batch.ts:342
    done --> discarded: markDiscarded batch.ts:342
    failed --> discarded: markDiscarded batch.ts:342

    confirmed --> [*]
    discarded --> [*]

    state "pg-boss job for extract-invoice" as boss {
        [*] --> created: enqueueExtraction queue.ts:62
        created --> active: boss.work batchSize 3 worker.ts:80
        active --> completed: handler returns completed<br/>extraction-worker.ts:441
        active --> retry: handler returns failed,<br/>retryLimit 2, retryDelay 30 s FIXED — no exponential backoff<br/>queue.ts:63-64
        retry --> active
        active --> deadletter: retries exhausted or expireInSeconds 600 elapsed<br/>deadLetter extract-invoice-dead-letter queue.ts:67
        deadletter --> dlq_row: drain worker writes dead_letter_queue<br/>worker.ts:158-179 · dead-letter.ts:148
        completed --> [*]
    }

    state "dead_letter_queue row, status pending" as dlq_row
    dlq_row --> replayed: MANUAL admin replay — extract-invoice only,<br/>needs source_id and restaurant_id<br/>admin/dead-letters/+page.server.ts:99-109
    dlq_row --> reviewed: MANUAL setStatus admin/dead-letters:78
    dlq_row --> purged: scheduled purge after<br/>DEAD_LETTER_PENDING_RETENTION_DAYS 180<br/>dead-letter.ts:12,388 · cron 20 3 * * * alerts.ts:1177
    replayed --> queued

    note right of dlq_row
        NO AUTOMATIC EXIT.
        normalize-product, categorize-product, whatsapp-notify and
        account-cleanup rows are not replayable at all — the replay
        action rejects any queue other than extract-invoice
        (admin/dead-letters/+page.server.ts:99). Their only exits are a
        human status change or the 180-day purge.
        No alert fires on growth: monitoring.md:70-71 names "above 0 / above
        10 in 24 h" for scheduled-job failures, and nothing in the repo
        wires a dead_letter_queue threshold to a pager.
    end note

    note right of failed
        WhatsApp-sourced items notify the sender
        (extraction-worker.ts:49) but have no retry
        affordance outside the web batch UI.
    end note

